## 🚀 Local Setup

### Prerequisites
- Node.js v18+ ([Download](https://nodejs.org))
- Python 3.9+ ([Download](https://python.org))
- Git
- MongoDB Atlas account (free) - [Create here](https://www.mongodb.com/cloud/atlas)

### Step 1: Clone & Install

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/parker.git
cd parker

# Install backend dependencies
npm install

# Install Python dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### Step 2: Environment Setup

Create a `.env` file in the root directory:

```env
# MongoDB
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://username:password@cluster.mongodb.net/parker?retryWrites=true&w=majority

# API Keys (get these from respective platforms)
TWITTER_BEARER_TOKEN=your_twitter_bearer_token
FACEBOOK_ACCESS_TOKEN=your_facebook_access_token

# App Settings
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=5000
FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:3000
SCRAPING_INTERVAL=3600  # 1 hour in seconds
LOG_LEVEL=info

# Email Notifications (Optional - Gmail)
SMTP_EMAIL=your_email@gmail.com
SMTP_PASSWORD=your_app_password

# Redis for background jobs (Optional for free tier - skip if not needed)
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379
```

### Step 3: Start the Application

```bash
# Terminal 1 - Backend
npm run dev

# Terminal 2 - Frontend
cd client
npm install
npm run dev

# Terminal 3 - Python Scraper (when ready)
python scripts/facebook_scraper.py
```

Backend will run on `http://localhost:5000`
Frontend will run on `http://localhost:3000`

